    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d901">

                <pb facs="1200" n="1190" sameAs="frus:frus1945v03/pg1190"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EW/3–2945: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-04-05T20:00:00-04:00">April 5, 1945—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1366. Bonnet has informed Department that his Government is much concerned over
                    delay in receiving invitation to join Reparations Commission.</p>
                <p>French already know of our approval (see Department’s 1229, March 29<anchor
                        n="40" xml:id="d901-f1"/>). Since Soviet, British and American governments
                    are all agreed on desirability of French participation and since Commission is
                    to function in Moscow, Ambassador Harriman has been instructed to inform Soviet
                    authorities that we expect them to extend the invitation to the French in behalf
                    of the participating governments.</p>
                <p>Please inform Bidault.<anchor n="41" xml:id="d901-f2"/> London is being asked to
                    inform Eden.<anchor n="42" xml:id="d901-f3"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d901-f1" n="40" xml:id="d901-f1-content">
                <p>See footnote 17, <ref target="#pg1179">p. 1179</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d901-f2" n="41" xml:id="d901-f2-content">
                <p>Georges Bidault, Minister for Foreign Affairs, Provisional Government of the
                    French Republic.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d901-f3" n="42" xml:id="d901-f3-content">
                <p>Anthony Eden, British Secretary of State for Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
